			<div id="content" class="site-content">
		<div class="ast-container">
				<div data-elementor-type="wp-page" data-elementor-id="365" class="elementor elementor-365" data-elementor-post-type="page">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d5829d51 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent" data-id="d5829d51" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-342e76bd elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="342e76bd" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					 <div class='gwd'> <header class='hero'> <div class='bg-mesh'><div class='blob blob1'></div><div class='blob blob2'></div><div class='blob blob3'></div></div> <div class='wrap hero-in'> <span class='pill'><i></i> Beauty Marketing Agency · Dubai</span> <h1>A beauty marketing agency for Dubai, where your next client <span class='hl'>may have landed this morning.</span></h1> <p class='sub'>Dubai salons and clinics sell to two audiences at once: a fast-growing resident population and millions of short-stay visitors, searching in English, Arabic, Russian and more. Glowth plans SEO, Google &amp; Meta ads, websites and AI booking around both audiences, district by district, and inside DHA advertising rules.</p> <div class='hero-ctas'> <a href='/get-a-free-audit/' class='btn btn-grad'>Get My Free Dubai Audit</a> <a href='#districts' class='btn btn-line'>See How Dubai Districts Differ</a> </div> <div class='stat-row'> <div class='stat-card'><b>19.59M</b><span>International overnight visitors to Dubai in 2025</span><small>Source: Dubai Department of Economy and Tourism (DET), 2025 annual figures</small></div> <div class='stat-card'><b>100%</b><span>Beauty-only agency: salons, clinics, spas</span></div> <div class='stat-card'><b>24/7</b><span>AI booking coverage available</span></div> </div> </div> </header> </div> 				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-1288e1aa elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="1288e1aa" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					 <div class='gwd'> <section> <div class='wrap'> <div> <span class='kicker'>The Dubai market, in numbers</span> <h2 style='margin-top:14px'>Two audiences, one booking calendar: <span class='hl'>residents and visitors</span></h2> </div> <div class='niche' style='margin-top:44px'> <div class='prose'> <p>Dubai ended 2025 with 4.58 million residents, a 7.5% rise in a single year, according to the Dubai Data and Statistics Establishment. That is roughly 330,000 new people in twelve months, all looking for a new hairdresser, nail tech, laser clinic or dermatologist. The practical effect for your salon or clinic: every month a fresh wave of residents has no loyalty yet, and they choose almost entirely through Google Maps, reviews and Instagram.</p> <small>Source: Dubai Data and Statistics Establishment, reported by The National, July 2026.</small> <h3>The daytime city is far bigger than the census</h3> <p>The same statistics office puts Dubai's peak daytime population at 6.39 million, including about 1.81 million temporary visitors in town for work or tourism. On top of that, the Department of Economy and Tourism counted 19.59 million international overnight visitors in 2025. Many of them book a blow-dry, nails, lashes or a facial during their stay, usually from a phone, often late at night, and often within walking or short taxi distance of their hotel. Campaigns that only target “people who live in Dubai” miss this audience entirely.</p> <small>Sources: Dubai Data and Statistics Establishment (via The National, 2026); DET 2025 visitor report (via Zawya, 2026).</small> <h3>Search happens in more than one language</h3> <p>DET's 2025 visitor mix shows why: Western Europe supplied 21% of visitors, while the CIS &amp; Eastern Europe, South Asia and the GCC each supplied about 15%, and the wider MENA region 11%. A Russian-speaking visitor searching for a manicure, or an Arabic-speaking family from the Gulf looking for a ladies' salon, does not type the English keywords your competitors bid on. We build separate ad groups, landing copy and Google Business Profile content for the languages your district actually hears. See our pages on <a href='/russian-beauty-salon/'>marketing a Russian-speaking beauty salon</a> and our <a href='/salon-marketing-dubai-guide/'>complete guide to getting more salon bookings in Dubai</a>.</p> <h3>What this changes in your marketing</h3> <p>For a Dubai business, budget planning has to follow both curves: steady resident demand, and visitor demand that rises and falls with hotel occupancy (80.7% on average across 2025, per DET). In practice that means always-on local SEO and Maps work for residents, plus flexible paid campaigns around hotels, malls and beach districts that you scale up when visitor demand is strong. If you want to see what that paid layer costs, read <a href='/salon-instagram-ads-cost-dubai/'>what a salon booking really costs on Instagram ads in Dubai</a>.</p> </div> <div class='niche-card'> <h3>Dubai at a glance</h3> <ul> <li><b>4.58M</b> residents at the end of 2025 (+7.5% year on year)</li> <li><b>6.39M</b> peak daytime population, incl. 1.81M temporary visitors</li> <li><b>19.59M</b> international overnight visitors in 2025</li> <li><b>15%</b> of 2025 visitors came from the CIS &amp; Eastern Europe</li> <li><b>80.7%</b> average hotel occupancy in 2025</li> </ul> <small>Sources: Dubai Data and Statistics Establishment (The National, 30 Jul 2026); Dubai Department of Economy and Tourism 2025 tourism performance (Zawya, 2026).</small> </div> </div> </div> </section> </div> 				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-b4e835b3 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="b4e835b3" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					 <div class='gwd'> <section style='background:#FBFAFE'> <div class='wrap'> <div class='center'> <span class='kicker'>Who regulates beauty in Dubai</span> <h2 style='margin-top:14px'>DHA, DHCR or Dubai Municipality: <span class='hl'>know whose rules your ads follow</span></h2> <p class='sub'>In Dubai, the regulator depends on what you offer and where you are licensed. A hair salon in Al Barsha and a filler clinic in Dubai Healthcare City answer to different authorities, so their marketing has different limits.</p> </div> <div class='svc-grid'> <div class='svc'> <span class='tagx'>Clinics &amp; medspas</span> <h3>Dubai Health Authority (DHA)</h3> <p>DHA licenses healthcare facilities and professionals in Dubai through its Sheryan system. Its Standards for Medical Advertisement Content on Social Media (September 2026) apply to licensed facilities, practitioners, staff and influencers. Key points:</p> <ul> <li>Content that names or identifies a facility needs the facility medical director's approval before posting</li> <li>Banned wording includes “the best”, “safest”, “100%”, “no side effects”, “guaranteed success” and “immediate results”</li> <li>Before/after images must show the same person, with no editing, and state that results vary</li> <li>Written patient consent is needed for any photo, video or testimonial</li> </ul> <small>Sources: DHA Sheryan licensing portal (dha.gov.ae); Gulf News and Communicate Online, September 2026.</small> </div> <div class='svc'> <span class='tagx'>Dubai Healthcare City</span> <h3>DHCR (Healthcare City Authority – Regulation)</h3> <p>Clinics licensed inside the Dubai Healthcare City free zone follow DHCR's own advertising policy. It covers print, video, press releases and social media posts, and requires an Advertising Review Request at least 14 working days before an ad runs.</p> <p>Approved ads must carry their approval number. Ads displayed outside the facility also need MOHAP approval after DHCR has approved them.</p> <small>Source: DHCR Advertising Policy (dhcc.ae).</small> </div> <div class='svc'> <span class='tagx'>Salons &amp; beauty centres</span> <h3>Dubai Municipality</h3> <p>Salons, barbershops, beauty centres and mobile salons follow Dubai Municipality's technical guideline DM-HSD-GU77 (version 4, issued January 2025), from the Health and Safety Department.</p> <p>This matters for marketing because the guideline bars salons from giving medical advice or offering unauthorised medical services. Non-surgical cosmetic services in a salon also need a permit under DHA requirements. So a salon ad should not promise treatments the licence does not cover.</p> <small>Source: Dubai Municipality, DM-HSD-GU77 Technical Guidelines for Compliance of Salons, Barbershops and Beauty Centers, V4 (dm.gov.ae).</small> </div> </div> <p class='note'>Every Glowth clinic campaign in Dubai is written and reviewed against the rules that apply to your licence before it goes live. For the full playbook, read our <a href='/clinic-marketing-uae-guide/'>guide to compliant aesthetic clinic marketing in the UAE</a>. This summary is general information, not legal advice; confirm specifics with your regulator.</p> </div> </section> </div> 				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-fe16f518 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="fe16f518" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					 <div class='gwd'> <section> <div class='wrap'> <div class='center'> <span class='kicker'>Services for Dubai businesses</span> <h2 style='margin-top:14px'>Nine services, each tuned to <span class='hl'>how Dubai books beauty</span></h2> <p class='sub'>Residents, hotel guests, multilingual searches and DHA rules: here is how each Glowth service adapts to the Dubai market.</p> </div> <div class='svc-grid'> <div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/seo-for-beauty-salons-clinics/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M4 19V5M4 19h16'/><path d='M8 15l3.5-4 3 2.5L19 8'/></svg></span><h3>Beauty Salon &amp; Clinic SEO in Dubai</h3><p>Pages and Google Business Profile content for the neighbourhood names Dubai people really type, from “JLT” to “Al Wasl”, plus Arabic and Russian versions where the district calls for it.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/salon-not-showing-google-maps/'>Read: Why a salon drops out of “near me” results →</a></div> <div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/google-ads-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><circle cx='11' cy='11' r='7'/><path d='M21 21l-4.3-4.3'/></svg></span><h3>Google Ads for Dubai Clinics &amp; Salons</h3><p>Separate campaigns for resident searches and for visitors searching around hotels and beach districts, so tourist clicks don't eat the budget meant for repeat local clients.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/clinic-google-ads-keywords/'>Read: The clinic keywords worth paying for →</a></div> <div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/instagram-facebook-ads-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M3 11l16-6-4 14-5-4-3 3v-5z'/></svg></span><h3>Instagram &amp; Facebook Ads in Dubai</h3><p>Meta audiences split by language and by “lives here” versus “visiting”, with clinic creative checked against DHA's social media advertising standards before launch.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/salon-instagram-ads-cost-dubai/'>Read: The honest cost of an Instagram booking in Dubai →</a></div> <div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/ai-appointment-booking-bot/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M21 12a8 8 0 0 1-8 8H4l2-3a8 8 0 1 1 15-5z'/></svg></span><h3>AI Booking Bot for Dubai</h3><p>Answers WhatsApp and web enquiries in several languages at any hour, useful when guests message from a different time zone or after your front desk has gone home.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/salon-whatsapp-booking-leak/'>Read: How bookings leak away after 7pm →</a></div> <div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/websites-landing-pages-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><rect x='3' y='4' width='18' height='13' rx='2'/><path d='M8 21h8M12 17v4'/></svg></span><h3>Websites for Dubai Beauty Brands</h3><p>Mobile-first sites with multilingual service pages, clear pricing and instant booking, built so a visitor can book from a hotel room without a phone call.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/salon-website-conversion-fixes/'>Read: 7 fixes that make a salon site take bookings →</a></div> <div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/social-media-management-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M12 3l1.8 4.6L18 9l-4.2 1.4L12 15l-1.8-4.6L6 9l4.2-1.4z'/><path d='M18 15l.9 2.1L21 18l-2.1.9L18 21l-.9-2.1L15 18l2.1-.9z'/></svg></span><h3>Social Media for Dubai Salons &amp; Clinics</h3><p>Content calendars that follow Dubai's own rhythm, from the cooler high season to Ramadan and summer, with captions written for the languages your clients speak.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/clinic-social-media-content-ideas-dha/'>Read: What clinics can post without before/afters →</a></div> <div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/ecommerce-for-beauty/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M6 7h12l1 13H5z'/><path d='M9 10V6a3 3 0 0 1 6 0v4'/></svg></span><h3>Ecommerce for Dubai Beauty Brands</h3><p>Online shops for retail ranges, gift cards and treatment packages that residents can reorder and visitors can buy before they fly home.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/salon-ecommerce-beauty-products/'>Read: Should your salon sell products online? →</a></div> <div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/reviews-reputation/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><path d='M12 3l2.7 5.5 6 .9-4.3 4.2 1 6-5.4-2.8L6.6 19.6l1-6L3.3 9.4l6-.9z'/></svg></span><h3>Reviews &amp; Reputation in Dubai</h3><p>A steady review system for a city where newcomers judge you on Google stars before they walk in, with replies in the reviewer's own language.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/clinic-bad-review-response-dha/'>Read: Answering a bad clinic review the DHA-safe way →</a></div> <div class='svc'><a class='svc-link' href='/services/'><span class='icw'><svg class='ico' viewBox='0 0 24 24'><rect x='3' y='3' width='18' height='18' rx='5'/><circle cx='12' cy='12' r='4'/><circle cx='17.2' cy='6.8' r='1'/></svg></span><h3>Dubai Growth Bundle</h3><p>One combined plan that balances always-on resident marketing with campaigns you scale up when visitor demand peaks, priced around your district and licence type.</p></a><a class='rd' href='/beauty-marketing-cost-dubai/'>Read: What beauty marketing costs in Dubai →</a></div> </div> </div> </section> </div> 				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-720f288b elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="720f288b" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					 <div class='gwd' id='gwd-dxb-districts'> <section class='district-sec' id='districts'> <div class='wrap'> <div class='center'> <span class='kicker' style='color:var(--lime)'>Interactive · Dubai district explorer</span> <h2 style='margin-top:14px;color:#fff'>Hotel guests in one district, <span style='color:var(--lime)'>families in the next.</span></h2> <p class='sub' style='color:#A7A2B6;margin:14px auto 0'>The resident-versus-visitor mix changes from one Dubai neighbourhood to the next. Tap a district to see how we would plan for it.</p> </div> <div class='district-tabs'> <button class='dtab on' data-d='marina'>Dubai Marina &amp; JBR</button> <button class='dtab' data-d='downtown'>Downtown &amp; Business Bay</button> <button class='dtab' data-d='jumeirah'>Jumeirah &amp; Umm Suqeim</button> <button class='dtab' data-d='difc'>DIFC</button> <button class='dtab' data-d='barsha'>Al Barsha &amp; JVC</button> <button class='dtab' data-d='deira'>Deira &amp; Al Karama</button> </div> <div class='dpanel on' data-p='marina'> <div><h3>Dubai Marina &amp; JBR</h3><p>Beach hotels and high-rise apartments side by side, so a salon here serves short-stay guests and long-term tenants in the same week. We split campaigns so visitor ads run in several languages near the hotels, while resident ads focus on repeat services and packages.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Hotel + resident mix</span><span>Multilingual searches</span><span>Walk-in and same-day demand</span></div></div> <div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Typical demand (Glowth view)</span><b>Nails, blow-dry, lashes, laser</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Main audience</span><b>Visitors and young residents</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Channel we lead with</span><b>Maps + Instagram</b></div></div> </div> <div class='dpanel' data-p='downtown'> <div><h3>Downtown &amp; Business Bay</h3><p>Office towers, serviced apartments and the Dubai Mall area bring a mix of busy professionals and visitors. Clinic and salon searches here are often made on the way to or from work, so clear pricing, easy parking or access notes, and fast online booking matter.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Office workers</span><span>Mall and hotel visitors</span><span>Booking speed matters</span></div></div> <div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Typical demand (Glowth view)</span><b>Injectables, facials, grooming</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Main audience</span><b>Professionals and visitors</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Channel we lead with</span><b>Google Search + SEO</b></div></div> </div> <div class='dpanel' data-p='jumeirah'> <div><h3>Jumeirah &amp; Umm Suqeim</h3><p>Villa communities with many long-term residents and established salons and clinics along Jumeirah Beach Road and Al Wasl Road. Clients here tend to stay with a business for years, so reviews, referrals and Arabic and English content carry more weight than discount ads.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Villa residents</span><span>Long-term loyalty</span><span>Arabic + English</span></div></div> <div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Typical demand (Glowth view)</span><b>Hair, skin, home-service beauty</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Main audience</span><b>Families and Emirati clients</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Channel we lead with</span><b>Reviews + local SEO</b></div></div> </div> <div class='dpanel' data-p='difc'> <div><h3>DIFC</h3><p>A financial district with a weekday working population. Appointments are squeezed between meetings, so the booking path has to work in a minute or two, and reminders have to fit a work calendar.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Weekday office crowd</span><span>Lunch and after-work slots</span><span>Short booking windows</span></div></div> <div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Typical demand (Glowth view)</span><b>Grooming, brows, skin</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Main audience</span><b>Finance and legal professionals</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Channel we lead with</span><b>AI booking + Google Ads</b></div></div> </div> <div class='dpanel' data-p='barsha'> <div><h3>Al Barsha &amp; Jumeirah Village Circle</h3><p>Residential communities where many of the city's newer residents settle. People who have just moved in are actively searching for a first salon or clinic nearby, which makes Maps visibility and a strong first-visit offer the most valuable assets.</p><div class='dtags'><span>New residents</span><span>Family areas</span><span>“Near me” searches</span></div></div> <div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Typical demand (Glowth view)</span><b>Hair, nails, kids' cuts, waxing</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Main audience</span><b>Families and new arrivals</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Channel we lead with</span><b>Local SEO + Maps</b></div></div> </div> <div class='dpanel' data-p='deira'> <div><h3>Deira &amp; Al Karama</h3><p>Older, dense neighbourhoods with many independent salons and a wide mix of nationalities. Clients compare prices and look for staff who speak their language, so we write listings and ads around services, prices and languages spoken.</p><div class='dtags'><span>Price-aware clients</span><span>Many languages</span><span>Dense, independent salons</span></div></div> <div class='dstats'><div class='dstat'><span>Typical demand (Glowth view)</span><b>Threading, henna, hair, grooming</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Main audience</span><b>Long-standing resident communities</b></div><div class='dstat'><span>Channel we lead with</span><b>Maps + WhatsApp</b></div></div> </div> <p class='dnote'>District notes are Glowth's qualitative view from working in the Dubai market, not measured search data. Your free audit checks the real figures for your location.</p> </div> </section> </div>  				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-8fc633ac elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="8fc633ac" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					 <div class='gwd'> <section style='background:#FBFAFE'> <div class='wrap'> <div class='center'> <span class='kicker'>Local search, Dubai style</span> <h2 style='margin-top:14px'>Be the map result a visitor <span class='hl'>taps from their hotel</span></h2> <p class='sub'>Someone who arrived yesterday doesn't know your name. They open Google Maps, type a service and a landmark, and choose from the first few pins. Your Google Business Profile, reviews and language options decide whether you are one of them.</p> </div> <div class='maps'> <div class='mhead'><span>Search: “manicure near JBR” — map results</span><em>Illustrative example</em></div> <div class='mrow you2'><span class='pin'>★</span><div><b>Your Salon</b><small>English · Arabic · Russian spoken · Open late · Online booking</small></div><span class='tag2'>GOAL</span></div> <div class='mrow'><span class='pin'>B</span><div><b>Nearby Salon B</b><small>Few recent reviews · No booking link</small></div></div> <div class='mrow'><span class='pin'>C</span><div><b>Nearby Salon C</b><small>Hours not updated · English only</small></div></div> </div> <p class='mnote'>This is an illustrative mock-up, not a real search result or client listing. It shows the profile details we optimise: languages spoken, opening hours, booking link and review freshness.</p> </div> </section> </div> 				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-d14e041a elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="d14e041a" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					 <div class='gwd'> <section> <div class='wrap'> <div class='center'> <span class='kicker'>Side by side</span> <h2 style='margin-top:14px'>Glowth compared with <span class='hl'>an all-industry Dubai agency</span></h2> </div> <div class='compare'> <div class='cmp-row cmp-head'><div></div><div class='glow'>Glowth</div><div>All-industry agency</div></div> <div class='cmp-row'><div>Resident vs. visitor audiences</div><div class='yes'>Planned and budgeted separately</div><div class='no'>One “Dubai” audience</div></div> <div class='cmp-row'><div>Arabic, Russian and other language campaigns</div><div class='yes'>Built where your district needs them</div><div class='no'>English only, or machine-translated</div></div> <div class='cmp-row'><div>DHA / DHCR advertising rules</div><div class='yes'>Checked before anything goes live</div><div class='no'>Found out after a complaint</div></div> <div class='cmp-row'><div>Salon vs. clinic licence limits (DM vs. DHA)</div><div class='yes'>Ads match what your licence allows</div><div class='no'>Same copy for every business</div></div> <div class='cmp-row'><div>Seasonality (high season, Ramadan, summer)</div><div class='yes'>Budget shifts planned in advance</div><div class='no'>Flat monthly spend</div></div> <div class='cmp-row'><div>What you get reported</div><div class='yes'>Bookings, by district and source</div><div class='no'>Clicks and impressions</div></div> <div class='cmp-row'><div>Contract terms</div><div class='yes'>Monthly rolling</div><div class='no'>Often 6–12 months</div></div> </div> </div> </section> </div> 				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e30dd85f elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="e30dd85f" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					 <div class='gwd'> <section> <div class='wrap'> <div class='center'> <span class='kicker'>Dubai FAQs</span> <h2 style='margin-top:14px'>Questions Dubai salon and clinic owners ask us</h2> </div> <div class='faq'> <details open><summary>Should a Dubai salon market to tourists or to residents?</summary><p>Usually both, but with separate campaigns. Dubai received 19.59 million international overnight visitors in 2025 (DET), while its resident population grew to 4.58 million. Residents bring repeat visits and long-term value; visitors bring one-off but often higher-spend bookings. We set separate budgets and targeting for each so one doesn't crowd out the other.</p></details> <details><summary>Do I need ads and listings in Arabic or Russian in Dubai?</summary><p>It depends on your district and clients. DET's 2025 figures show visitors came from Western Europe, the CIS and Eastern Europe, South Asia, the GCC and wider MENA in large numbers, so many searches are not in English. If your staff serve clients in those languages, adding matching ad groups, landing pages and profile details usually reaches people your English-only competitors miss. See our <a href='/russian-beauty-salon/'>Russian-speaking salon marketing page</a>.</p></details> <details><summary>Does a Dubai clinic need approval before posting ads on Instagram?</summary><p>Under DHA's social media advertising standards (September 2026), content that names or identifies a DHA-licensed facility must be approved by the facility's medical director before it is published, and claims like “100%”, “no side effects” or “guaranteed” are not allowed. Clinics licensed in Dubai Healthcare City follow DHCR's advertising policy, which requires a review request at least 14 working days before the ad runs. Our <a href='/clinic-marketing-uae-guide/'>clinic marketing guide</a> covers this in more detail.</p></details> <details><summary>Can a beauty salon in Dubai advertise laser or skin treatments?</summary><p>Only if it is licensed to provide them. Dubai Municipality's salon guideline (DM-HSD-GU77, January 2025) says salons and beauty centres must not give medical advice or offer unauthorised medical services, and non-surgical cosmetic services need a permit under DHA requirements. If you offer laser or injectables, that part of the business is marketed as a licensed clinic service. Learn more on our <a href='/laser-hair-removal-clinics/'>laser hair removal clinic marketing page</a>.</p></details> <details><summary>How do bookings that arrive after closing time get handled?</summary><p>Phorest's analysis of more than 5,000 salons and spas found that 46% of appointments were booked outside opening hours. In Dubai, where visitors may message from another time zone, we connect an AI booking assistant to WhatsApp and your website so these enquiries get an answer and a slot straight away instead of the next morning.</p></details> </div> </div> </section> </div> 				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-c7016f97 elementor-widget elementor-widget-html" data-id="c7016f97" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="html.default">
					 <div class='gwd'> <div class='cov'><div class='wrap'> <p>Popular Dubai specialities</p> <div class='cov-links'> <a href='/russian-beauty-salon/'>Russian-speaking salons →</a> <a href='/laser-hair-removal-clinics/'>Laser hair removal clinics →</a> <a href='/medical-spas/'>Medspas →</a> <a href='/aesthetic-clinics/'>Aesthetic clinics →</a> </div> <p>Also in the UAE</p> <div class='cov-links'> <a href='/abu-dhabi/'>Salon &amp; clinic marketing in Abu Dhabi →</a> <a href='/sharjah/'>Salon &amp; clinic marketing in Sharjah →</a> </div> </div></div> </div> 				</div>
